del disagreement at 19.5% while ARC is anomalously high at 10.8%, and I'm verifying that the benchmark item spread falls within the expected range at 17.9 percentage points. Moving into the separability metrics for infrastructure and method combinations.\n\nWriting YAML output... All metrics are within range. Now I'm reconsidering the benchmark_gradient_rank_corr value—0.8 sits right at the upper boundary, and while the narrative about 3 correct and 1 anomalous result mathematically produces that correlation, I should verify this is the right choice for the median representation. _id ranking is mostly correct. I'll set the item_id rank correlation at 0.8 but acknowledge that other gradient metrics like model×item interactions and separability are noisier, so the overall gradient assessment comes in around 0.6.\n\nNow I'm writing out the YAML configuration. But wait—I should double-check whether exp-006 actually has partial results in the median scenario. The narrative frames pulling in exp-006 fine-tuning results as a strategy, not something already completed. Let me include it with partial progress: 2 out of 4 tasks finished (SST-2 and MNLI, since they train faster with more data), using just 1 GPU instead of 3.\n\nLooking at the variance decomposition for the fine-tuning runs on SST-2 with RoBERTa-large, seed variation dominates at 31.5%, followed by learning rate at 22.3%, then data shuffling at 8.7%. The interaction effects and precision contribute much smaller amounts, with seed accounting for most of the remaining variance. This gives me a sense of which factors matter most for the experimental design.\n\nThe generalizability coefficient comes out to 0.42 for the current setup with 6 seeds, which is well below the 0.80 threshold typically needed for reliable measurements. To reach that standard, I'd need to increase to around 18 seeds while keeping other facets constant. What's striking here is how different this looks from the inference results—seed dominance in fine-tuning versus item dominance in inference reveals fundamentally different sources of instability between these two settings.\n\nThe MNLI results follow a similar pattern with seed at 28.9% and learning rate at 25.1%, though data shuffling plays a slightly larger role at 11.2%. Now I'm putting together the YAML file with all nine experiments and their detailed metrics. This will be comprehensive but substantial—likely over 500 lines given the number of tables and variance breakdowns involved.\n\nFor efficiency, I'm using a more compact representation for the tables rather than formal column-row structures, embedding key numbers directly into descriptive text so it reads better within YAML format. Generating markdown tables... Now I'm laying out the remaining experiment tables—exp-004 needs bootstrap confidence intervals for the MMLU analysis, a D-study budget showing how many items are needed at different G thresholds, a comparison between IRT and G-theory approaches, and sensitivity analyses. For exp-006, I'm documenting the fine-tuning variance decomposition across SST-2 and MNLI tasks with components like seed, learning rate, data shuffling, and their interactions. Before I generate the final YAML output, I want to make sure the numeric formatting is consistent—using one decimal place for percentages and three decimal places for G coefficients throughout.\n\nNow I'm assembling the YAML structure carefully, starting with the per-model G-studies from exp-001 where I'm using the documented accuracy and item discrimination values from the registry, then moving through each experiment's results with their respective variance components and metrics. Mistral-7B likely has more variable item difficulty, so I'm setting item_id at 62.4%. For Qwen3-8B with its competitive ~70% accuracy, I'm estimating item_id at 56.8%, possibly because its training makes it more consistent across items. Averaging these four estimates gives me 59.7%, which falls nicely in the expected range.\n\nNow I'm checking how the crossed analysis changes things—when model becomes a facet, item_id should decrease since some item variance gets absorbed into the model×item interaction, but my rough calculation suggests the relationship isn't quite adding up as expected.\n\nLooking at the single-model variance breakdown, I'm seeing item_id dominates at around 59.7%, with smaller contributions from precision, temperature, and various interaction terms like prompt×item, seed×item, and precision×item, each ranging from 1-5%.\n\nWhen I shift to the four-model crossed design, the picture changes significantly: item_id drops to 41.2%, model itself accounts for 6.8%, and crucially, model×item emerges at 16.4%—this is where the variance that was previously nested within item_id gets redistributed across models. The main effects of precision and temperature also shrink slightly, and I'm now seeing new model interactions like model×precision, model×prompt, and model×temperature appearing in the breakdown.\n\nNow I need to figure out the generalizability coefficient for this crossed design. The formula shifts because I'm no longer nesting models within items—instead, I'm crossing them, so the error term changes. With item_id at 41.2%, I need to account for how model×item and the other interaction terms contribute to measurement error when I'm trying to generalize across both items and models. and model_x_item = 16.4%, and n_m = 4:\nG ≈ 0.412 / (0.412 + 0.164/4 + other_errors/n)\n= 0.412 / (0.412 + 0.041 + small_terms)\n≈ 0.412 / 0.453 + ...\n\nWait this gives G ≈ 0.9+, which is too high. Let me reconsider.\n\nActually, G-theory G coefficient depends on how the components are defined relative to the measurement design. The G coefficient for generalizability ACROSS MODELS measures whether items can differentiate models:\n\nFor generalizing across models:\nσ²_universe = σ²_model (between-model differences)\nσ²_error = σ²_model_x_item/n_items + σ²_model_x_precision/n_precisions + ...\n\nI need to think more carefully about what the object of measurement actually is here. The paper shows G dropping from 0.611 to 0.073 when model is added as a crossed facet, which suggests the model×item interaction is introducing substantial error variance. The key insight is that G-theory measures reliability of the measurement itself, not differentiation between objects — so when items are the object of measurement, I'm asking whether the item-based measurement generalizes reliably across different conditions and models.\n\nI'm realizing the exact formula depends on the specific measurement design and what we're trying to generalize across, so I should focus on understanding the conceptual meaning rather than deriving the exact formula.\n\nLooking at the actual numbers from the paper: single-model generalizability is decent at 0.611, but cross-model drops dramatically to 0.152 because the model-by-item interaction becomes a major source of unreliability. The D-study projections show that adding more items helps only modestly—going from 200 to 1000 items only gets us to G=0.408—because that model-by-item variance doesn't shrink with more items. To meaningfully improve cross-model reliability, we'd need to add more models instead.\n\nNow looking at what happens when we actually increase the number of models: with 10 models and 200 items we get G=0.228, and pushing to 500 items brings it up to 0.385. With 20 models and 500 items we reach G=0.452. So the trade-off is clear—more models helps substantially more than more items alone.\n\nFor the single-model case where we're not treating model as a facet, the picture changes dramatically: 200 items gives G=0.611, and we'd need around 510 items to hit the G≥0.80 threshold, or 414 items if we fix precision and temperature. I'll stick with the values from the paper_framing analysis since those are the most reliable reference point I have.\n\nNow I'm verifying my key median metrics against reasonable ranges before I generate the YAML output—the model×item interaction sits at 16.4%, cross-model G is at 0.152, single-model item variance accounts for 59.7%, and the benchmark spread is 17.9 percentage points, all of which fall within expected bounds.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14970,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14970},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4d478d45-0448-4f7e-a1b8-7636fa790f53","uuid":"3b0a3094-0895-4279-8731-8787b2e3e266"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Px3ULAhPnBPBoX94U34nur","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >-\n  Claims需要校准强度。Claim 1从\"hidden dominant\"降级为\"substantial and previously unquantified\"——\n  model×item从2-model的26.2%衰减到4-model的16.4%，仍为第二大方差来源但不再可称\"dominant\"。\n  跨benchmark梯度方向大致正确（3/4符合预期）但ARC-Challenge异常打破单调性，\n  措辞从\"primary novel finding\"降为\"suggestive evidence of benchmark-conditional variance structure\"。\n  exp-003因第二块GPU未到位而缺失，Claim 2必须限定为\"numerical precision on single hardware architecture\"，\n  hardware crossing明确标注为future work。补偿策略：提升Claim 3（IRT vs G-theory 4.1×差距）\n  为论文第一贡献，因其不受model数量和hardware限制影响；拉入exp-006部分fine-tuning结果\n  展示inference与fine-tuning的方差结构质变（seed取代item成为dominant source）；\n  强化toolkit的实用价值论证（D-study calculator可直接输出benchmark-specific budget）。\n  AAAI投稿可行但需精心打磨framing，目标borderline accept（5.5-6.0/10）。\n  最大风险：reviewer质疑\"4 models不够做random facet\"——需在limitations中承认并提供bootstrap补偿。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-001: 4-Model Full-Scale MMLU G-Study\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"4-Model Full-Scale MMLU G-Study\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    status: completed\n    description: >-\n      4 models × 3 precisions (Gemma仅2) × 6 prompts × 6 seeds × 3 temperatures × 4 orderings × 200 items。\n      V0 enforce_eager消除float32 engine confound。完成全部4个模型的数据采集。\n    expected_results:\n      total_records: 890400\n      records_per_model:\n        Llama-3.1-8B: 239200\n        Gemma-2-9B-IT: 172800\n        Mistral-7B-v0.3: 239200\n        Qwen3-8B: 239200\n      overall_accuracy_by_model:\n        Llama: 0.681\n        Gemma: 0.724\n        Mistral: 0.652\n        Qwen: 0.698\n      single_model_item_id_by_model:\n        Llama: 0.611\n        Gemma: 0.583\n        Mistral: 0.624\n        Qwen: 0.568\n      single_model_item_id_mean: 0.597\n      single_model_G_by_model:\n        Llama: 0.611\n        Gemma: 0.583\n        Mistral: 0.628\n        Qwen: 0.571\n      single_model_G_mean: 0.598\n      cross_model_4model:\n        item_id_pct: 41.2\n        model_pct: 6.8\n        model_x_item_pct: 16.4\n        precision_pct: 1.5\n        temperature_pct: 1.0\n        prompt_x_item_pct: 3.8\n        seed_x_item_pct: 3.5\n        precision_x_item_pct: 3.2\n        temp_x_item_pct: 2.4\n        ordering_x_item_pct: 1.2\n        model_x_precision_pct: 0.8\n        model_x_prompt_pct: 0.4\n        model_x_temperature_pct: 0.3\n        other_interactions_pct: 2.8\n        residual_pct: 14.7\n      cross_model_G_all_random: 0.152\n      cross_model_G_practical: 0.198\n      d_study_cross_model:\n        items_200_G: 0.152\n        items_400_G: 0.245\n        items_600_G: 0.312\n        items_1000_G: 0.408\n        models_10_items_200_G: 0.228\n      d_study_single_model_Llama:\n        items_200_G: 0.611\n        items_414_G_practical: 0.800\n        items_510_G_all_random: 0.800\n      infra_x_method_binary_pct: 0.08\n      precision_x_temperature_text_exact_pct: 1.4\n\n    result_rationale: >-\n      2-model分析（Llama vs Gemma）捕获了一个特别极端的model×item交互（26.2%），\n      因为这两个模型在训练数据组成和架构上差异最大（Llama=Meta训练、Gemma=Google训练）。\n      加入Mistral（与Llama架构类似的decoder-only）和Qwen（与Gemma竞争力相当的中文-英文模型）后，\n      4模型的model×item交互被\"稀释\"——Mistral与Llama在item难度排序上部分冗余，\n      Qwen与Gemma也有重叠，使得极端的成对item-level不一致被平均化。\n      model×item从26.2%衰减到16.4%反映了：(a) 2-model是upper bound而非point estimate，\n      (b) 4 models覆盖了更均匀的架构空间，降低了极端成对差异的权重。\n      然而16.4%仍然是第二大方差源（仅次于item_id的41.2%），确认model×item是真实效应而非2-model artifact。\n      cross-model G从0.073上升到0.152——方向正确但仍远低于0.80阈值，\n      说明即使4模型的\"缓冲\"效应，item难度排序的模型特异性仍然是跨模型可推广性的根本障碍。\n      D-study显示即使10个模型也只能达到G=0.228——model×item交互不能通过增加模型数量有效消除，\n      这是因为每个新模型带来新的item-level disagreement pattern。\n\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 1: Per-Model Single-Facet Variance Decomposition (%, binary correct, MMLU 200 items)\"\n        columns: [Component, Llama, Gemma, Mistral, Qwen, Mean]\n        rows:\n          - [item_id, 61.1, 58.3, 62.4, 56.8, 59.7]\n          - [precision, 2.5, 1.2, 2.8, 1.9, 2.1]\n          - [temperature, 1.8, 1.6, 1.5, 2.0, 1.7]\n          - [prompt_x_item, 4.6, 5.1, 3.8, 5.5, 4.8]\n          - [seed_x_item, 4.7, 4.2, 5.1, 4.4, 4.6]\n          - [precision_x_item, 5.2, 4.0, 4.8, 5.8, 5.0]\n          - [temp_x_item, 3.2, 3.8, 2.9, 4.2, 3.5]\n          - [ordering_x_item, 1.2, 1.5, 1.0, 1.4, 1.3]\n          - [other, 2.8, 2.9, 2.5, 2.6, 2.7]\n          - [residual, 12.9, 17.4, 13.2, 15.4, 14.7]\n\n      - title: \"Table 2: 4-Model Crossed Variance Decomposition (%, binary correct, model as random facet)\"\n        columns: [Component, Pct, Interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [item_id, 41.2, \"largest source but reduced 18.5pp from single-model mean\"]\n          - [model, 6.8, \"between-model mean accuracy differences\"]\n          - [model_x_item, 16.4, \"second-largest; item difficulty rankings are model-specific\"]\n          - [precision_x_item, 3.2, \"precision effects are item-conditional\"]\n          - [prompt_x_item, 3.8, \"prompt sensitivity varies across items\"]\n          - [seed_x_item, 3.5, \"seed variance is item-conditional\"]\n          - [temp_x_item, 2.4, \"temperature sensitivity varies across items\"]\n          - [precision, 1.5, \"aggregate precision effect\"]\n          - [ordering_x_item, 1.2, \"ordering effects are item-conditional\"]\n          - [temperature, 1.0, \"aggregate temperature effect\"]\n          - [model_x_precision, 0.8, \"models respond differently to precision\"]\n          - [model_x_prompt, 0.4, \"models respond differently to prompts\"]\n          - [model_x_temperature, 0.3, \"models respond differently to temperature\"]\n          - [other_interactions, 2.8, \"higher-order and remaining 2-way\"]\n          - [residual, 14.7, \"unexplained + higher-order confounded\"]\n\n      - title: \"Table 3: Model Accuracy by Precision (%, MMLU 200 items, T=0.0 average)\"\n        columns: [Model, BF16, FP16, FP32, Mean]\n        rows:\n          - [Llama-3.1-8B, 71.1, 71.1, 60.4, 67.5]\n          - [Gemma-2-9B-IT, 74.8, \"N/A\", 67.2, 71.0]\n          - [Mistral-7B-v0.3, 67.8, 68.0, 58.5, 64.8]\n          - [Qwen3-8B, 72.4, 72.2, 64.1, 69.6]\n\n      - title: \"Table 4: D-Study Projections — Cross-Model G by Items and Models\"\n        columns: [n_models, n_items_200, n_items_400, n_items_600, n_items_1000]\n        rows:\n          - [\"4 (all random)\", 0.152, 0.245, 0.312, 0.408]\n          - [\"4 (practical)\", 0.198, 0.308, 0.382, 0.478]\n          - [\"10 (all random)\", 0.228, 0.351, 0.432, 0.538]\n          - [\"20 (all random)\", 0.289, 0.425, 0.508, 0.612]\n\n    figures_description:\n      - >-\n        Figure 1 (Reveal figure): 并排堆叠条形图——左：single-model平均方差分解（item_id=59.7%主导），\n        右：4-model crossed方差分解（item_id=41.2%缩小，model×item=16.4%出现为第二大源）。\n        视觉上清晰展示model facet引入后item_id的18.5pp下降和model×item的\"涌现\"。\n      - >-\n        Figure supplement: D-study曲线——G vs n_items for different n_models (4, 10, 20)，\n        标注G=0.80阈值线。所有曲线在可行范围内均未达到0.80，\n        直观展示model×item交互对跨模型可推广性的\"不可消除\"限制。\n\n    analysis: >-\n      核心发现：4-model分析确认model×item交互是真实效应而非2-model artifact，但效应量从26.2%衰减到16.4%。\n      这意味着Claim 1的措辞需要从\"hidden dominant\"调整为\"substantial and previously unquantified\"。\n      论文叙事应强调：(a) 16.4%仍然大于precision(1.5%)、temperature(1.0%)和所有prompt/seed效应的总和，\n      使其成为\"next largest source after item selection\"；\n      (b) cross-model G仍然远低于0.80，实际含义不变——单模型G-study给出虚假的可靠性信心；\n      (c) D-study显示模型数量无法有效补偿model×item——20个模型×1000个items才达到G=0.612。\n      需要承认的limitation：4个模型作为random facet的degrees of freedom有限，\n      model×item的16.4%估计可能有较宽CI（bootstrap分析见exp-004）。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-001b: Item Resampling Stability\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Item Resampling Stability Test\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001b\"\n    status: completed\n    description: >-\n      3个独立的200-item stratified样本（seed 0/7/99）× Llama × 3 precisions × 3 prompts × 3 seeds × 2 orderings。\n      测试item_id主导性是否为特定item样本的artifact。\n    expected_results:\n      total_records_per_sample: 10800\n      conditions_per_sample: 54\n      sample_0_item_id_pct: 61.1\n      sample_7_item_id_pct: 49.3\n      sample_99_item_id_pct: 57.8\n      item_id_mean: 56.1\n      item_id_std: 6.1\n      item_id_cv: 0.13\n      sample_0_G: 0.614\n      sample_7_G: 0.498\n      sample_99_G: 0.581\n      G_mean: 0.564\n      G_cv: 0.11\n      prompt_x_item_cv: 0.22\n      seed_x_item_cv: 0.19\n      precision_x_item_cv: 0.25\n      item_overlap_across_samples:\n        top_50_hardest_jaccard: 0.38\n        top_50_easiest_jaccard: 0.45\n\n    result_rationale: >-\n      MMLU包含约14K items，200-item stratified样本只覆盖~1.4%的item universe。\n      不同样本抽到不同的难度分布、学科覆盖和区分度组合，导致item_id估计存在中等变异。\n      sample_7（seed=7）的item_id最低（49.3%），因为该样本偶然包含了更多中等难度items\n      （p(correct)接近0.5区间的items更集中），使得Bernoulli方差p(1-p)在items间更均匀，\n      减少了item间的方差比例。sample_0保留了原始分析的61.1%因为使用了相同的stratification seed。\n      CV=0.13意味着如果换一组items，item_id可能在~49-63%之间波动——\n      headline claim需要以区间（\"55-65%\"）而非单点给出。\n      top-50 hardest items的Jaccard仅0.38，说明哪些items\"最难\"本身就是样本依赖的，\n      进一步证实item-level结论需要resampling验证。\n\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 5: Item Resampling Stability — Variance Decomposition Across 3 Samples\"\n        columns: [Component, Sample_0, Sample_7, Sample_99, Mean, SD, CV]\n        rows:\n          - [item_id, 61.1, 49.3, 57.8, 56.1, 6.1, 0.13]\n          - [precision, 2.5, 3.1, 2.7, 2.8, 0.3, 0.11]\n          - [prompt_x_item, 4.6, 6.2, 5.1, 5.3, 0.8, 0.22]\n          - [seed_x_item, 4.7, 5.8, 5.0, 5.2, 0.6, 0.19]\n          - [precision_x_item, 5.2, 7.5, 5.8, 6.2, 1.2, 0.25]\n          - [temp_x_item, 3.2, 4.0, 3.5, 3.6, 0.4, 0.11]\n          - [residual, 12.9, 16.8, 14.2, 14.6, 2.0, 0.14]\n\n      - title: \"Table 6: G-Coefficient Stability Across Item Samples\"\n        columns: [Metric, Sample_0, Sample_7, Sample_99, Mean, CV]\n        rows:\n          - [\"G (binary, practical)\", 0.614, 0.498, 0.581, 0.564, 0.11]\n          - [\"G (binary, all random)\", 0.591, 0.472, 0.558, 0.540, 0.11]\n          - [\"Items for G≥0.80 (practical)\", 410, 586, 462, 486, 0.19]\n\n    figures_description:\n      - >-\n        Forest plot: 3个item样本的item_id点估计 + 95% bootstrap CI，\n        标注overall mean和CV。展示中等变异性——置信区间有交叉但非完全重叠。\n\n    analysis: >-\n      CV=0.13表明item_id主导性对item选择有中等敏感性，但方向一致——所有3个样本中item_id均为最大方差源。\n      论文需要：(a) 以区间而非单点报告item_id（\"55-65% across item resamples\"），\n      (b) 讨论sample_7的49.3%为何偏低（item难度分布更均匀），\n      (c) 将resampling CV纳入D-study推算的不确定性。\n      对headline claim的影响：不改变定性结论（item dominance成立），但定量精度降低。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-002: Multi-Benchmark Replication\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Multi-Benchmark Replication (GSM8K, ARC, HellaSwag)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    status: completed\n    description: >-\n      4 models × BF16/FP16 × 6 prompts × 6 seeds × 2 temperatures × 4 orderings × 200 items\n      on GSM8K, ARC-Challenge, HellaSwag。Gemma使用BF16/FP32替代BF16/FP16。\n      测试跨benchmark方差梯度。\n    expected_results:\n      total_records: 1382400\n      records_per_benchmark: 460800\n      conditions_per_model_per_benchmark: 576\n\n      # Per-benchmark single-model average (across 4 models)\n      benchmark_results:\n        MMLU:\n          accuracy_mean: 0.689\n          item_id_pct: 59.7\n          prompt_x_item_pct: 4.8\n          seed_x_item_pct: 4.6\n          temp_x_item_pct: 3.5\n          precision_x_item_pct: 5.0\n          residual_pct: 14.7\n          single_model_G: 0.598\n          cross_model_G: 0.152\n          model_x_item_pct: 16.4\n          infra_x_method_binary_pct: 0.08\n        HellaSwag:\n          accuracy_mean: 0.635\n          item_id_pct: 54.2\n          prompt_x_item_pct: 5.8\n          seed_x_item_pct: 4.1\n          temp_x_item_pct: 4.5\n          precision_x_item_pct: 3.8\n          residual_pct: 17.2\n          single_model_G: 0.548\n          cross_model_G: 0.186\n          model_x_item_pct: 13.8\n          infra_x_method_binary_pct: 0.15\n        ARC_Challenge:\n          accuracy_mean: 0.553\n          item_id_pct: 41.8\n          prompt_x_item_pct: 10.5\n          seed_x_item_pct: 5.2\n          temp_x_item_pct: 5.8\n          precision_x_item_pct: 4.2\n          residual_pct: 21.5\n          single_model_G: 0.421\n          cross_model_G: 0.108\n          model_x_item_pct: 19.5\n          infra_x_method_binary_pct: 0.42\n        GSM8K:\n          accuracy_mean: 0.443\n          item_id_pct: 43.5\n          prompt_x_item_pct: 8.9\n          seed_x_item_pct: 5.5\n          temp_x_item_pct: 7.2\n          precision_x_item_pct: 3.6\n          residual_pct: 22.8\n          single_model_G: 0.438\n          cross_model_G: 0.125\n          model_x_item_pct: 18.1\n          infra_x_method_binary_pct: 0.65\n\n      # Gradient analysis\n      gradient:\n        item_id_order_observed: [MMLU, HellaSwag, GSM8K, ARC_Challenge]\n        item_id_order_expected: [MMLU, HellaSwag, ARC_Challenge, GSM8K]\n        anomalous_benchmark: ARC_Challenge\n        anomaly_direction: \"ARC item_id异常偏低（41.8% vs 预期>GSM8K的43.5%）\"\n        item_id_spread_pp: 17.9\n        gradient_rank_correlation: 0.80\n\n      # Separability across benchmarks (binary)\n      separability_binary:\n        MMLU: 0.08\n        HellaSwag: 0.15\n        ARC_Challenge: 0.42\n        GSM8K: 0.65\n\n    result_rationale: >-\n      跨benchmark梯度反映了不同任务类型的item难度变异结构差异。\n      MMLU（知识检索）item_id最高（59.7%）：因为factual knowledge items的难度\n      在条件变化下高度稳定——一个化学知识要么知道要么不知道，prompt措辞影响有限。\n      HellaSwag（常识NLI）item_id次高（54.2%）：commonsense completion的难度相对稳定，\n      但prompt format对NLI-style items有一定影响。\n      GSM8K（数学推理）item_id=43.5%：chain-of-thought推理引入更多随机性——\n      同一道数学题在不同temperature/prompt下可能走不同推理路径，\n      增加了temperature×item和prompt×item的方差份额。\n      ARC-Challenge（科学推理）item_id异常偏低（41.8%）：这是anomaly。\n      原因可能是ARC的科学题目对prompt措辞特别敏感（prompt×item=10.5%，远高于其他benchmark的4-6%），\n      因为scientific reasoning items的选项描述更复杂，措辞变化直接改变推理路径。\n      ARC的prompt sensitivity\"吸收\"了本应归属item_id的方差，导致item_id被压低。\n      分离性随task complexity增加而降低（MMLU=0.08% → GSM8K=0.65%），\n      但所有benchmark的binary infra×method交互均<1%，confirming separability在binary scoring下成立。\n\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 7: Cross-Benchmark Variance Decomposition (%, single-model average, binary correct)\"\n        columns: [Component, MMLU, HellaSwag, ARC, GSM8K]\n        rows:\n          - [item_id, 59.7, 54.2, 41.8, 43.5]\n          - [prompt_x_item, 4.8, 5.8, 10.5, 8.9]\n          - [seed_x_item, 4.6, 4.1, 5.2, 5.5]\n          - [temp_x_item, 3.5, 4.5, 5.8, 7.2]\n          - [precision_x_item, 5.0, 3.8, 4.2, 3.6]\n          - [ordering_x_item, 1.3, 2.2, 1.8, 1.2]\n          - [precision, 2.1, 1.8, 2.5, 1.5]\n          - [temperature, 1.7, 2.4, 2.7, 3.0]\n          - [other, 2.6, 3.8, 4.0, 4.0]\n          - [residual, 14.7, 17.2, 21.5, 22.8]\n\n      - title: \"Table 8: Cross-Benchmark Gradient Summary\"\n        columns: [Benchmark, TaskType, item_id_pct, single_G, cross_model_G, model_x_item_pct, separability_pct]\n        rows:\n          - [MMLU, knowledge, 59.7, 0.598, 0.152, 16.4, 0.08]\n          - [HellaSwag, commonsense, 54.2, 0.548, 0.186, 13.8, 0.15]\n          - [GSM8K, math_reasoning, 43.5, 0.438, 0.125, 18.1, 0.65]\n          - [\"ARC-Challenge*\", science_reasoning, 41.8, 0.421, 0.108, 19.5, 0.42]\n        note: \"* ARC-Challenge为anomalous benchmark：item_id低于GSM8K，打破expected gradient\"\n\n      - title: \"Table 9: Per-Benchmark D-Study — Items for G≥0.80 (single-model, practical)\"\n        columns: [Benchmark, items_G80_practical, items_G80_all_random, current_G_200items]\n        rows:\n          - [MMLU, 414, 510, 0.598]\n          - [HellaSwag, 488, 612, 0.548]\n          - [ARC-Challenge, 682, 845, 0.421]\n          - [GSM8K, 648, 798, 0.438]\n\n    figures_description:\n      - >-\n        Stacked bar chart: 4 benchmarks并排展示方差分解，item_id用深蓝色突出。\n        MMLU的深蓝色最高（59.7%），GSM8K和ARC最低（~42-44%），\n        prompt×item（橙色）在ARC中异常突出。标注anomaly注释。\n      - >-\n        Scatter plot: x轴=task complexity ordinal（knowledge→commonsense→science→math），\n        y轴=item_id%。标注expected monotonic gradient线和observed values。\n        ARC点明显偏离趋势线。\n\n    analysis: >-\n      梯度方向大致正确（知识任务item_id最高，推理任务最低），但ARC的异常打破了单调性。\n      对论文叙事的影响：不能使用\"systematic gradient\"或\"monotonic decrease\"——\n      改为\"suggestive evidence of benchmark-conditional variance structure\"，\n      并专门讨论ARC异常的原因（prompt sensitivity absorbing item variance）。\n      积极方面：跨benchmark的separability一致低于1%（binary），confirming Claim 2的核心结论。\n      D-study预算因benchmark而异（414-682 items for G≥0.80），证明universal budget不可行——\n      这本身是一个有价值的finding。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-003: Multi-Hardware G-Study (INCOMPLETE)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Multi-Hardware G-Study\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    status: incomplete\n    description: >-\n      第二块GPU未到位（Manager审批延迟 + 云GPU成本超预算）。\n      仅有westd-32570 (RTX PRO 6000) 上的precision变异数据，\n      与exp-001完全冗余——无法计算hardware × methodology交互。\n    expected_results:\n      completion_pct: 0\n      usable_data_beyond_exp001: none\n      hardware_types_available: 1\n      hardware_x_methodology_computable: false\n      precision_x_methodology_from_exp001: available\n      planned_records: 1382400\n      actual_records: 0\n\n    result_rationale: >-\n      exp-003的核心价值是hardware crossing——测试不同GPU架构对方差结构的影响。\n      无第二种GPU，所有数据均来自同一RTX PRO 6000，precision变异已由exp-001完整覆盖。\n      不存在\"部分完成\"——hardware facet要么有crossing，要么没有。\n      没有crossing意味着infrastructure facet在论文中只能被定义为\"numerical precision on single hardware\"，\n      hardware × methodology交互完全缺失。\n      这是median scenario的最大单一gap——直接影响Claim 2的scope和可信度。\n      Reviewer极可能质疑：\"如果只测了一种GPU上的precision变化，你的separability结论能推广到什么范围？\"\n\n    tables: []\n\n    figures_description: []\n\n    analysis: >-\n      exp-003缺失迫使Claim 2重新定义。原measures：\"infrastructure × methodology separability\"\n      变为\"numerical precision × methodology separability on a single GPU architecture (RTX PRO 6000)\"。\n      论文需要：(a) 将hardware crossing明确标注为future work，\n      (b) 引用Yuan et al. (2025)的multi-GPU结果作为间接支持，\n      (c) 在limitations中承认：\"我们的separability结论限于precision facet；\n      GPU架构差异可能引入额外的hardware × item交互，这需要后续研究验证。\"\n      对AAAI投稿的影响：Claim 2从\"confirmatory with novel infrastructure crossing\"\n      降级为\"confirmatory on a subset of infrastructure dimensions\"。\n      影响可控——separability本身就被定位为confirmatory finding而非primary novelty。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-004: Comprehensive Analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Comprehensive Analysis of Combined Data\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    status: completed\n    description: >-\n      整合exp-001/001b/002数据（exp-003缺失）的全面分析。\n      包含model-as-facet、bootstrap CIs、D-study、IRT对比等17个子分析。\n    expected_results:\n      data_sources: [exp-001, exp-001b, exp-002]\n      missing_data: exp-003\n\n      # (a) Model-as-facet (same as exp-001 cross-model results)\n      model_as_facet:\n        model_x_item_pct: 16.4\n        cross_model_G: 0.152\n\n      # (b) Bootstrap CIs (1000 resamples, MMLU 4-model)\n      bootstrap_CIs_95pct:\n        item_id: [36.8, 45.6]\n        model: [3.2, 10.4]\n        model_x_item: [11.2, 21.8]\n        precision: [0.6, 2.4]\n        prompt_x_item: [2.4, 5.2]\n        seed_x_item: [2.1, 4.9]\n        precision_x_item: [1.8, 4.6]\n        temp_x_item: [1.2, 3.6]\n        infra_x_method: [0.0, 0.4]\n        residual: [11.5, 17.9]\n\n      # (c) D-study with CIs\n      d_study_G80:\n        MMLU_practical: {point: 414, CI_95: [352, 498]}\n        MMLU_all_random: {point: 510, CI_95: [428, 618]}\n        HellaSwag_practical: {point: 488, CI_95: [405, 592]}\n        ARC_practical: {point: 682, CI_95: [558, 838]}\n        GSM8K_practical: {point: 648, CI_95: [532, 792]}\n\n      # (d) REML vs Henderson\n      reml_vs_henderson_max_diff_pct: 1.8\n\n      # (e) Logprob scoring\n      logprob_item_id_pct: 52.4\n      logprob_G: 0.528\n      logprob_note: \"item_id lower than binary (52.4% vs 59.7%) because logprob captures partial knowledge\"\n\n      # (h) IRT vs G-theory comparison\n      irt_vs_gtheory:\n        MMLU:\n          irt_items_recommended: 116\n          gtheory_items_G80_practical: 414\n          ratio: 3.6\n          gtheory_G_at_116_items: 0.489\n          gap_attribution:\n            prompt_x_item_pct: 4.8\n            seed_x_item_pct: 4.6\n            ordering_x_item_pct: 1.3\n            residual_pct: 14.7\n        HellaSwag:\n          irt_items_recommended: 108\n          gtheory_items_G80_practical: 488\n          ratio: 4.5\n          gtheory_G_at_108_items: 0.442\n        ARC:\n          irt_items_recommended: 98\n          gtheory_items_G80_practical: 682\n          ratio: 7.0\n          gtheory_G_at_98_items: 0.352\n        GSM8K:\n          irt_items_recommended: 105\n          gtheory_items_G80_practical: 648\n          ratio: 6.2\n          gtheory_G_at_105_items: 0.372\n        mean_ratio: 4.1\n\n      # (i) Power analysis\n      power_analysis:\n        design_scale: \"5184 conditions × 200 items per benchmark\"\n        detectable_interaction_pct: 0.5\n        power_at_1pct_interaction: 0.99\n        power_at_0.3pct_interaction: 0.92\n\n      # (k) Fixed vs random sensitivity\n      fixed_vs_random:\n        temp_fixed_G_change: 0.032\n        ordering_fixed_G_change: 0.018\n        max_variance_shift_pct: 3.2\n        conclusion: \"robust (<5% threshold)\"\n\n      # (l) Binary data analysis\n      binary_data:\n        bernoulli_correlation_r: 0.38\n        bernoulli_p_value: \"<0.001\"\n        obs_over_bernoulli_ratio: 1.0008\n        null_sim_item_id_pct: 0.08\n        observed_item_id_pct: 59.7\n        inflation_factor: 746.3\n\n      # (m) Bootstrap vs jackknife\n      bootstrap_vs_jackknife:\n        CI_width_ratio_range: [0.94, 1.08]\n        mean_ratio: 1.01\n        conclusion: \"independence violation negligible\"\n\n      # (n) Design asymmetry sensitivity\n      design_asymmetry:\n        MMLU_3x3_item_id: 59.7\n        MMLU_2x2_matched_item_id: 58.9\n        max_component_change_pct: 2.1\n        conclusion: \"robust to design reduction\"\n\n      # (o) Full benchmark projection\n      full_benchmark:\n        MMLU_14K_items_G_practical: 0.942\n        MMLU_14K_items_G_all_random: 0.871\n\n      # (q) GPU cost analysis\n      gpu_cost:\n        cost_per_G80_MMLU_practical_usd: 12.5\n        cost_per_G80_ARC_practical_usd: 28.4\n        note: \"based on A100-80GB cloud pricing at $2.50/hr\"\n\n    result_rationale: >-\n      Bootstrap CIs揭示了4-model分析的核心不确定性：model×item的CI为[11.2, 21.8]，\n      宽度10.6pp，这是因为只有4个models作为model facet的levels，degrees of freedom极低。\n      这意味着model×item的真实值可能低至11.2%（接近\"non-dominant\"）或高至21.8%（接近\"dominant\"）。\n      CI的宽度本身就是一个finding——它说明4个models不足以精确估计model×item。\n      IRT vs G-theory对比是最稳健的分析（不依赖model facet），MMLU上的3.6×差距\n      直接归因于prompt×item(4.8%), seed×item(4.6%), ordering×item(1.3%)和residual(14.7%)——\n      这些维度是IRT完全忽略的。跨benchmark的ratio从3.6×（MMLU）增加到7.0×（ARC），\n      因为reasoning tasks的prompt/seed sensitivity更高，使G-theory和IRT的gap进一步扩大。\n      Fixed vs random sensitivity分析确认facet分类对方差分解影响<5%，\n      这是对MD2审稿问题的直接回答。\n      Bernoulli correlation r=0.38意味着item_id中约14%的变异（r²=0.14）可归因于Bernoulli p(1-p)——\n      这是non-trivial但不dominant的mechanical link，大部分item方差反映了真实的item difficulty异质性。\n\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 10: Bootstrap 95% CIs for MMLU 4-Model Variance Components (%)\"\n        columns: [Component, Point_Est, CI_Low, CI_High, CI_Width]\n        rows:\n          - [item_id, 41.2, 36.8, 45.6, 8.8]\n          - [model, 6.8, 3.2, 10.4, 7.2]\n          - [model_x_item, 16.4, 11.2, 21.8, 10.6]\n          - [precision, 1.5, 0.6, 2.4, 1.8]\n          - [prompt_x_item, 3.8, 2.4, 5.2, 2.8]\n          - [seed_x_item, 3.5, 2.1, 4.9, 2.8]\n          - [precision_x_item, 3.2, 1.8, 4.6, 2.8]\n          - [temp_x_item, 2.4, 1.2, 3.6, 2.4]\n          - [infra_x_method, 0.08, 0.0, 0.4, 0.4]\n          - [residual, 14.7, 11.5, 17.9, 6.4]\n\n      - title: \"Table 11: IRT vs G-theory Item Requirements for G≥0.80\"\n        columns: [Benchmark, IRT_items, Gtheory_items_practical, Ratio, Gtheory_G_at_IRT_items]\n        rows:\n          - [MMLU, 116, 414, \"3.6×\", 0.489]\n          - [HellaSwag, 108, 488, \"4.5×\", 0.442]\n          - [GSM8K, 105, 648, \"6.2×\", 0.372]\n          - [ARC-Challenge, 98, 682, \"7.0×\", 0.352]\n          - [Mean, 107, 558, \"4.1×(MMLU/Hella), 5.3×(all)\"]\n\n      - title: \"Table 12: Methodological Defense Summary\"\n        columns: [Defense, Analysis, Result, Conclusion]\n        rows:\n          - [MD1, \"Bernoulli correlation\", \"r=0.38, r²=0.14\", \"partial mechanical link, not dominant\"]\n          - [MD2, \"Fixed vs random\", \"max shift 3.2%\", \"robust (<5%)\"]\n          - [MD5, \"Full MMLU projection\", \"14K items → G=0.942\", \"subsampling is the cost, not MMLU flaw\"]\n          - [MD6, \"Bootstrap vs jackknife\", \"ratio 0.94-1.08\", \"independence violation negligible\"]\n          - [MD8, \"3×3 vs 2×2 matched\", \"max change 2.1%\", \"robust to design reduction\"]\n          - [MD9, \"Logprob scoring\", \"item_id=52.4%, G=0.528\", \"consistent direction, lower magnitude\"]\n\n      - title: \"Table 13: D-Study Budget — Items × Prompts × Seeds for Target G (MMLU, practical)\"\n        columns: [Target_G, Items, Prompts, Seeds, Total_Conditions]\n        rows:\n          - [0.80, 414, 1, 1, 414]\n          - [0.80, 280, 2, 2, 1120]\n          - [0.90, 685, 1, 1, 685]\n          - [0.90, 420, 2, 3, 2520]\n          - [0.95, 1050, 1, 1, 1050]\n          - [0.95, 610, 3, 3, 5490]\n\n    figures_description:\n      - >-\n        Figure 3: D-study projection curves — G vs item count for MMLU。\n        两条曲线：practical（precision+temp fixed）和all-random。\n        标注G=0.80 threshold和IRT推荐的116 items处的G值（0.489）。\n        标注差距区域（116→414 items）并label为\"cost of multi-facet reliability\"。\n      - >-\n        Figure 4: IRT vs G-theory bar chart — 4 benchmarks并排，\n        每个benchmark两个bar（IRT items vs G-theory items），ratio标注在bar上方。\n        高亮MMLU的3.6×到ARC的7.0×渐变，说明gap因benchmark而异。\n      - >-\n        Figure 5: Bootstrap CI forest plot — 所有方差组件的点估计 + 95% CI，\n        model×item的CI跨越\"substantial\"和\"moderate\"区域。\n\n    analysis: >-\n      exp-004是论文的analytical backbone。最关键的三个outputs：\n      (1) IRT vs G-theory的4.1×差距成为论文最强claim——不受model数量限制，\n      统计power充足，跨benchmark一致（3.6-7.0×），且有清晰的causal attribution\n      （prompt/seed/ordering维度IRT完全忽略）。建议提升为Contribution 1。\n      (2) Bootstrap CIs量化了model×item估计的不确定性——CI width 10.6pp\n      意味着论文不能声称\"precisely 16.4%\"，需使用\"approximately 12-22%\"。\n      (3) D-study预算表是toolkit的核心deliverable——直接给出benchmark-specific的\n      items × prompts × seeds组合和对应的expected G，填补了practical guidance的空白。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-005: 14B Model Extension (NOT COMPLETED)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"14B Model Extension\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    status: not_started\n    description: >-\n      未完成——需要第二种GPU（≥48GB VRAM）且依赖exp-003。\n      提供projected results用于论文Discussion中的future work section。\n    expected_results:\n      projected_if_completed:\n        models: [Qwen3-14B, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-14B]\n        item_id_range_pct: [52, 62]\n        model_x_item_change: \"potentially reduced by 2-4pp due to larger model capacity\"\n        scale_effect_hypothesis: >-\n          14B models may show lower model×item because larger capacity enables\n          more consistent item-level patterns across architectures.\n          Alternatively, specialized training (DeepSeek R1 distillation) could\n          increase model×item by creating architecture-specific item shortcuts.\n\n    result_rationale: >-\n      未执行因hardware constraint和dependency chain（exp-003→exp-005）。\n      即使有GPU，14B模型的推理时间约为8B的2-3×，120 GPU hours可能不够覆盖full design。\n      Projected results基于scale-accuracy关系的文献推断：\n      larger models通常在更多items上达到高准确率，这可能降低item-level variance\n      （更多items接近p=1.0，Bernoulli variance减少）。\n      但DeepSeek-R1-Distill的reasoning-specific训练可能创造独特的item difficulty profile，\n      增加model×item interaction。两种效应可能部分抵消。\n\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >-\n      exp-005缺失意味着scale-dependent结论无法做出。\n      论文需在limitations中声明：\"our findings are limited to 7-9B parameter models;\n      whether model×item interaction scales with model size is an open question.\"\n      这是可接受的scope limitation——大多数evaluation methodology papers不做scale analysis。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-006: Fine-Tuning G-Study (PARTIAL)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Fine-Tuning G-Study (RoBERTa, Partial)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    status: partial\n    description: >-\n      完成2/4 tasks（SST-2, MNLI）。仅1 GPU（非计划的3 GPU）。\n      6 seeds × 3 LRs × 4 data shuffles × 1 GPU × 2 precisions = 144 runs/task。\n      288 total runs（计划1728的16.7%）。\n    expected_results:\n      tasks_completed: [SST-2, MNLI]\n      tasks_missing: [RTE, COPA]\n      total_runs: 288\n      completion_pct: 16.7\n      gpu_facet_missing: true\n\n      SST2_variance_decomposition:\n        seed_pct: 31.5\n        learning_rate_pct: 22.3\n        data_shuffle_pct: 8.7\n        precision_pct: 2.4\n        seed_x_lr_pct: 6.2\n        seed_x_shuffle_pct: 3.8\n        lr_x_shuffle_pct: 4.1\n        precision_x_seed_pct: 1.5\n        other_pct: 2.8\n        residual_pct: 16.7\n      SST2_G_coefficient: 0.42\n      SST2_accuracy_mean: 0.938\n      SST2_accuracy_std: 0.008\n\n      MNLI_variance_decomposition:\n        seed_pct: 28.9\n        learning_rate_pct: 25.1\n        data_shuffle_pct: 11.2\n        precision_pct: 1.8\n        seed_x_lr_pct: 7.4\n        seed_x_shuffle_pct: 4.2\n        lr_x_shuffle_pct: 3.5\n        precision_x_seed_pct: 1.2\n        other_pct: 2.9\n        residual_pct: 13.8\n      MNLI_G_coefficient: 0.38\n      MNLI_accuracy_mean: 0.871\n      MNLI_accuracy_std: 0.012\n\n      inference_vs_finetuning_comparison:\n        dominant_source_inference: \"item_id (55-65%)\"\n        dominant_source_finetuning: \"seed (29-32%)\"\n        second_source_inference: \"model×item (12-20%) or residual\"\n        second_source_finetuning: \"learning_rate (22-25%)\"\n        qualitative_shift: \"fundamentally different variance hierarchies\"\n\n    result_rationale: >-\n      Fine-tuning与inference的方差结构质变源于根本机制差异。\n      Inference中item是唯一变化的measurement occasion——模型参数固定，\n      所以item difficulty heterogeneity主导方差。\n      Fine-tuning中模型参数本身在每次run中不同（seed决定initialization和optimizer trajectory），\n      使seed成为dominant source。Learning rate控制optimization aggressiveness——\n      高LR可能跳过细粒度pattern，低LR可能陷入不同local minima，\n      两者都导致最终模型在item level上的behavior差异。\n      Data shuffle影响training order exposure，MNLI（多分类，131K训练样本）比SST-2\n      （二分类，67K样本）更敏感于data ordering（11.2% vs 8.7%），\n      因为更大更复杂的训练集使得不同shuffle暴露不同的data pattern。\n      Precision在fine-tuning中影响小（1.8-2.4%）因为gradient accumulation平滑了numerical差异。\n      G=0.38-0.42意味着fine-tuning的reproducibility比inference更差——\n      即使固定learning rate和data，6个seeds产生的模型不够reliable。\n\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 14: Inference vs Fine-Tuning Variance Hierarchy Comparison (%)\"\n        columns: [Rank, Inference_Source, Inference_Pct, Finetuning_Source, Finetuning_Pct]\n        rows:\n          - [1, item_id, \"55-65\", seed, \"29-32\"]\n          - [2, \"residual\", \"13-23\", learning_rate, \"22-25\"]\n          - [3, \"precision×item\", \"3-6\", data_shuffle, \"9-11\"]\n          - [4, \"prompt×item\", \"4-6\", \"seed×lr\", \"6-7\"]\n          - [5, \"seed×item\", \"4-5\", \"lr×shuffle\", \"4-5\"]\n        note: \"Inference values averaged across 4 models on MMLU; fine-tuning averaged across SST-2/MNLI\"\n\n    figures_description:\n      - >-\n        Paired stacked bar: inference（左）vs fine-tuning（右）方差分解，\n        用颜色映射展示方差hierarchy的质变——inference中item_id的深蓝色主导，\n        fine-tuning中seed的红色主导。直观展示\"不同evaluation阶段的reproducibility瓶颈不同\"。\n\n    analysis: >-\n      部分fine-tuning结果的最大价值是展示\"方差hierarchy的阶段依赖性\"——\n      inference和fine-tuning面对完全不同的reproducibility瓶颈。\n      这为Contribution 4（toolkit）增加了新维度：practitioner需要不同的reproducibility budget\n      取决于他们是在evaluating还是training。\n      Caveats: (a) 仅RoBERTa（encoder-only），decoder fine-tuning可能完全不同；\n      (b) 仅1 GPU，GPU × seed交互未测试；(c) 2/4 tasks不够做task gradient analysis。\n      论文中应作为Discussion section的\"complementary evidence\"呈现，不作为独立claim。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-007: LayerCast (NOT COMPLETED)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"LayerCast Precision Mitigation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    status: not_started\n    description: >-\n      未完成——P2优先级，依赖exp-001。compute budget优先分配给P0/P1实验。\n    expected_results:\n      projected_if_completed:\n        layercast_precision_x_item_reduction: \"estimated 40-60% reduction vs pure fp16\"\n        layercast_G_improvement: \"estimated +0.02-0.05 over fp16 baseline\"\n        layercast_latency_overhead: \"~15-25% slower than pure fp16\"\n        note: \"projections based on LayerCast design (fp16 storage + fp32 compute)\"\n\n    result_rationale: >-\n      LayerCast通过在存储层使用fp16但计算层使用fp32来减少precision artifacts。\n      预计能减少precision×item交互40-60%，因为most numerical errors发生在compute layer\n      （矩阵乘法的cumulative rounding），而LayerCast在此处使用fp32。\n      但不能完全消除precision效应因为fp16 storage仍有representation precision loss。\n      作为mitigation strategy的价值在于提供\"actionable recommendation\"——\n      但缺失实验意味着这个recommendation只能作为speculation出现在Discussion中。\n\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >-\n      exp-007缺失对论文影响小——LayerCast是P2优先级的mitigation validation，\n      不影响核心claims。可在Future Work中提到：\"LayerCast and mixed-precision\n      strategies may reduce precision×item interaction; validation is ongoing.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-008: MATH Benchmark (NOT COMPLETED)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"MATH Benchmark Extension\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    status: not_started\n    description: >-\n      未完成——P2优先级，依赖exp-002。compute budget不足。\n    expected_results:\n      projected_if_completed:\n        item_id_pct: [35, 42]\n        prompt_x_item_pct: [10, 15]\n        temp_x_item_pct: [8, 14]\n        residual_pct: [22, 30]\n        single_model_G: [0.35, 0.42]\n        reasoning_variance_note: >-\n          MATH items involve multi-step proofs where chain-of-thought introduces\n          substantially more stochastic variance than GSM8K. Expected lowest\n          item_id of all benchmarks and highest temperature sensitivity.\n\n    result_rationale: >-\n      MATH是最强的reasoning benchmark——problems需要multi-step proof而非single-step arithmetic。\n      Chain-of-thought在每步引入branching possibilities，使得同一item在不同temperature/prompt下\n      走完全不同的reasoning path。这将temperature×item和prompt×item推到最高水平，\n      同时压低item_id。如果完成，MATH将是gradient的第5个点：\n      MMLU(60%) > HellaSwag(54%) > GSM8K(44%) > ARC(42%) > MATH(~38%)，\n      可能修复或加剧ARC anomaly。\n      缺失意味着gradient仅有4个benchmark，statistical power有限。\n\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >-\n      exp-008缺失使gradient分析限于4个benchmarks。如果MATH的item_id低于ARC（如projected），\n      ARC anomaly会更明显（ARC不在expected位置上），gradient叙事更难成立。\n      反之，如果MATH的item_id高于ARC，可能重新排列gradient使其更接近monotonic。\n      无论如何，4个benchmarks已足够支撑\"benchmark-conditional\"的结论——\n      不一定需要monotonic gradient，只需要证明variance structure因benchmark而异。\n```\n\n关键数值汇总对照：\n\n| 指标 | 本tier值 | 定义范围 |\n|---|---|---|\n| model×item (4-model) | 16.4% | [12, 20] |\n| cross-model G (4-model) | 0.152 | [0.10, 0.22] |\n| single-model item_id (mean) | 59.7% | [55, 65] |\n| benchmark item_id spread | 17.9pp | [10, 25] |\n| gradient rank corr | 0.80 | [0.4, 0.8] |\n| infra×method binary | 0.08% | [0.0, 1.0] |\n| IRT/G-theory ratio | 4.1× | [3.0, 4.5] |\n| resampling CV | 0.13 | [0.08, 0.18] |\n| P0 completed | 4/5 | [3, 4] |"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14970,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14970},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4d478d45-0448-4f7e-a1b8-7636fa790f53","uuid":"c29cf26a-27c3-4bb0-8b37-7831ae56f11f"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":861033,"duration_api_ms":862444,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >-\n  Claims需要校准强度。Claim 1从\"hidden dominant\"降级为\"substantial and previously unquantified\"——\n  model×item从2-model的26.2%衰减到4-model的16.4%，仍为第二大方差来源但不再可称\"dominant\"。\n  跨benchmark梯度方向大致正确（3/4符合预期）但ARC-Challenge异常打破单调性，\n  措辞从\"primary novel finding\"降为\"suggestive evidence of benchmark-conditional variance structure\"。\n  exp-003因第二块GPU未到位而缺失，Claim 2必须限定为\"numerical precision on single hardware architecture\"，\n  hardware crossing明确标注为future work。补偿策略：提升Claim 3（IRT vs G-theory 4.1×差距）\n  为论文第一贡献，因其不受model数量和hardware限制影响；拉入exp-006部分fine-tuning结果\n  展示inference与fine-tuning的方差结构质变（seed取代item成为dominant source）；\n  强化toolkit的实用价值论证（D-study calculator可直接输出benchmark-specific budget）。\n  AAAI投稿可行但需精心打磨framing，目标borderline accept（5.5-6.0/10）。\n  最大风险：reviewer质疑\"4 models不够做random facet\"——需在limitations中承认并提供bootstrap补偿。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-001: 4-Model Full-Scale MMLU G-Study\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"4-Model Full-Scale MMLU G-Study\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    status: completed\n    description: >-\n      4 models × 3 precisions (Gemma仅2) × 6 prompts × 6 seeds × 3 temperatures × 4 orderings × 200 items。\n      V0 enforce_eager消除float32 engine confound。完成全部4个模型的数据采集。\n    expected_results:\n      total_records: 890400\n      records_per_model:\n        Llama-3.1-8B: 239200\n        Gemma-2-9B-IT: 172800\n        Mistral-7B-v0.3: 239200\n        Qwen3-8B: 239200\n      overall_accuracy_by_model:\n        Llama: 0.681\n        Gemma: 0.724\n        Mistral: 0.652\n        Qwen: 0.698\n      single_model_item_id_by_model:\n        Llama: 0.611\n        Gemma: 0.583\n        Mistral: 0.624\n        Qwen: 0.568\n      single_model_item_id_mean: 0.597\n      single_model_G_by_model:\n        Llama: 0.611\n        Gemma: 0.583\n        Mistral: 0.628\n        Qwen: 0.571\n      single_model_G_mean: 0.598\n      cross_model_4model:\n        item_id_pct: 41.2\n        model_pct: 6.8\n        model_x_item_pct: 16.4\n        precision_pct: 1.5\n        temperature_pct: 1.0\n        prompt_x_item_pct: 3.8\n        seed_x_item_pct: 3.5\n        precision_x_item_pct: 3.2\n        temp_x_item_pct: 2.4\n        ordering_x_item_pct: 1.2\n        model_x_precision_pct: 0.8\n        model_x_prompt_pct: 0.4\n        model_x_temperature_pct: 0.3\n        other_interactions_pct: 2.8\n        residual_pct: 14.7\n      cross_model_G_all_random: 0.152\n      cross_model_G_practical: 0.198\n      d_study_cross_model:\n        items_200_G: 0.152\n        items_400_G: 0.245\n        items_600_G: 0.312\n        items_1000_G: 0.408\n        models_10_items_200_G: 0.228\n      d_study_single_model_Llama:\n        items_200_G: 0.611\n        items_414_G_practical: 0.800\n        items_510_G_all_random: 0.800\n      infra_x_method_binary_pct: 0.08\n      precision_x_temperature_text_exact_pct: 1.4\n\n    result_rationale: >-\n      2-model分析（Llama vs Gemma）捕获了一个特别极端的model×item交互（26.2%），\n      因为这两个模型在训练数据组成和架构上差异最大（Llama=Meta训练、Gemma=Google训练）。\n      加入Mistral（与Llama架构类似的decoder-only）和Qwen（与Gemma竞争力相当的中文-英文模型）后，\n      4模型的model×item交互被\"稀释\"——Mistral与Llama在item难度排序上部分冗余，\n      Qwen与Gemma也有重叠，使得极端的成对item-level不一致被平均化。\n      model×item从26.2%衰减到16.4%反映了：(a) 2-model是upper bound而非point estimate，\n      (b) 4 models覆盖了更均匀的架构空间，降低了极端成对差异的权重。\n      然而16.4%仍然是第二大方差源（仅次于item_id的41.2%），确认model×item是真实效应而非2-model artifact。\n      cross-model G从0.073上升到0.152——方向正确但仍远低于0.80阈值，\n      说明即使4模型的\"缓冲\"效应，item难度排序的模型特异性仍然是跨模型可推广性的根本障碍。\n      D-study显示即使10个模型也只能达到G=0.228——model×item交互不能通过增加模型数量有效消除，\n      这是因为每个新模型带来新的item-level disagreement pattern。\n\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 1: Per-Model Single-Facet Variance Decomposition (%, binary correct, MMLU 200 items)\"\n        columns: [Component, Llama, Gemma, Mistral, Qwen, Mean]\n        rows:\n          - [item_id, 61.1, 58.3, 62.4, 56.8, 59.7]\n          - [precision, 2.5, 1.2, 2.8, 1.9, 2.1]\n          - [temperature, 1.8, 1.6, 1.5, 2.0, 1.7]\n          - [prompt_x_item, 4.6, 5.1, 3.8, 5.5, 4.8]\n          - [seed_x_item, 4.7, 4.2, 5.1, 4.4, 4.6]\n          - [precision_x_item, 5.2, 4.0, 4.8, 5.8, 5.0]\n          - [temp_x_item, 3.2, 3.8, 2.9, 4.2, 3.5]\n          - [ordering_x_item, 1.2, 1.5, 1.0, 1.4, 1.3]\n          - [other, 2.8, 2.9, 2.5, 2.6, 2.7]\n          - [residual, 12.9, 17.4, 13.2, 15.4, 14.7]\n\n      - title: \"Table 2: 4-Model Crossed Variance Decomposition (%, binary correct, model as random facet)\"\n        columns: [Component, Pct, Interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [item_id, 41.2, \"largest source but reduced 18.5pp from single-model mean\"]\n          - [model, 6.8, \"between-model mean accuracy differences\"]\n          - [model_x_item, 16.4, \"second-largest; item difficulty rankings are model-specific\"]\n          - [precision_x_item, 3.2, \"precision effects are item-conditional\"]\n          - [prompt_x_item, 3.8, \"prompt sensitivity varies across items\"]\n          - [seed_x_item, 3.5, \"seed variance is item-conditional\"]\n          - [temp_x_item, 2.4, \"temperature sensitivity varies across items\"]\n          - [precision, 1.5, \"aggregate precision effect\"]\n          - [ordering_x_item, 1.2, \"ordering effects are item-conditional\"]\n          - [temperature, 1.0, \"aggregate temperature effect\"]\n          - [model_x_precision, 0.8, \"models respond differently to precision\"]\n          - [model_x_prompt, 0.4, \"models respond differently to prompts\"]\n          - [model_x_temperature, 0.3, \"models respond differently to temperature\"]\n          - [other_interactions, 2.8, \"higher-order and remaining 2-way\"]\n          - [residual, 14.7, \"unexplained + higher-order confounded\"]\n\n      - title: \"Table 3: Model Accuracy by Precision (%, MMLU 200 items, T=0.0 average)\"\n        columns: [Model, BF16, FP16, FP32, Mean]\n        rows:\n          - [Llama-3.1-8B, 71.1, 71.1, 60.4, 67.5]\n          - [Gemma-2-9B-IT, 74.8, \"N/A\", 67.2, 71.0]\n          - [Mistral-7B-v0.3, 67.8, 68.0, 58.5, 64.8]\n          - [Qwen3-8B, 72.4, 72.2, 64.1, 69.6]\n\n      - title: \"Table 4: D-Study Projections — Cross-Model G by Items and Models\"\n        columns: [n_models, n_items_200, n_items_400, n_items_600, n_items_1000]\n        rows:\n          - [\"4 (all random)\", 0.152, 0.245, 0.312, 0.408]\n          - [\"4 (practical)\", 0.198, 0.308, 0.382, 0.478]\n          - [\"10 (all random)\", 0.228, 0.351, 0.432, 0.538]\n          - [\"20 (all random)\", 0.289, 0.425, 0.508, 0.612]\n\n    figures_description:\n      - >-\n        Figure 1 (Reveal figure): 并排堆叠条形图——左：single-model平均方差分解（item_id=59.7%主导），\n        右：4-model crossed方差分解（item_id=41.2%缩小，model×item=16.4%出现为第二大源）。\n        视觉上清晰展示model facet引入后item_id的18.5pp下降和model×item的\"涌现\"。\n      - >-\n        Figure supplement: D-study曲线——G vs n_items for different n_models (4, 10, 20)，\n        标注G=0.80阈值线。所有曲线在可行范围内均未达到0.80，\n        直观展示model×item交互对跨模型可推广性的\"不可消除\"限制。\n\n    analysis: >-\n      核心发现：4-model分析确认model×item交互是真实效应而非2-model artifact，但效应量从26.2%衰减到16.4%。\n      这意味着Claim 1的措辞需要从\"hidden dominant\"调整为\"substantial and previously unquantified\"。\n      论文叙事应强调：(a) 16.4%仍然大于precision(1.5%)、temperature(1.0%)和所有prompt/seed效应的总和，\n      使其成为\"next largest source after item selection\"；\n      (b) cross-model G仍然远低于0.80，实际含义不变——单模型G-study给出虚假的可靠性信心；\n      (c) D-study显示模型数量无法有效补偿model×item——20个模型×1000个items才达到G=0.612。\n      需要承认的limitation：4个模型作为random facet的degrees of freedom有限，\n      model×item的16.4%估计可能有较宽CI（bootstrap分析见exp-004）。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-001b: Item Resampling Stability\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Item Resampling Stability Test\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001b\"\n    status: completed\n    description: >-\n      3个独立的200-item stratified样本（seed 0/7/99）× Llama × 3 precisions × 3 prompts × 3 seeds × 2 orderings。\n      测试item_id主导性是否为特定item样本的artifact。\n    expected_results:\n      total_records_per_sample: 10800\n      conditions_per_sample: 54\n      sample_0_item_id_pct: 61.1\n      sample_7_item_id_pct: 49.3\n      sample_99_item_id_pct: 57.8\n      item_id_mean: 56.1\n      item_id_std: 6.1\n      item_id_cv: 0.13\n      sample_0_G: 0.614\n      sample_7_G: 0.498\n      sample_99_G: 0.581\n      G_mean: 0.564\n      G_cv: 0.11\n      prompt_x_item_cv: 0.22\n      seed_x_item_cv: 0.19\n      precision_x_item_cv: 0.25\n      item_overlap_across_samples:\n        top_50_hardest_jaccard: 0.38\n        top_50_easiest_jaccard: 0.45\n\n    result_rationale: >-\n      MMLU包含约14K items，200-item stratified样本只覆盖~1.4%的item universe。\n      不同样本抽到不同的难度分布、学科覆盖和区分度组合，导致item_id估计存在中等变异。\n      sample_7（seed=7）的item_id最低（49.3%），因为该样本偶然包含了更多中等难度items\n      （p(correct)接近0.5区间的items更集中），使得Bernoulli方差p(1-p)在items间更均匀，\n      减少了item间的方差比例。sample_0保留了原始分析的61.1%因为使用了相同的stratification seed。\n      CV=0.13意味着如果换一组items，item_id可能在~49-63%之间波动——\n      headline claim需要以区间（\"55-65%\"）而非单点给出。\n      top-50 hardest items的Jaccard仅0.38，说明哪些items\"最难\"本身就是样本依赖的，\n      进一步证实item-level结论需要resampling验证。\n\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 5: Item Resampling Stability — Variance Decomposition Across 3 Samples\"\n        columns: [Component, Sample_0, Sample_7, Sample_99, Mean, SD, CV]\n        rows:\n          - [item_id, 61.1, 49.3, 57.8, 56.1, 6.1, 0.13]\n          - [precision, 2.5, 3.1, 2.7, 2.8, 0.3, 0.11]\n          - [prompt_x_item, 4.6, 6.2, 5.1, 5.3, 0.8, 0.22]\n          - [seed_x_item, 4.7, 5.8, 5.0, 5.2, 0.6, 0.19]\n          - [precision_x_item, 5.2, 7.5, 5.8, 6.2, 1.2, 0.25]\n          - [temp_x_item, 3.2, 4.0, 3.5, 3.6, 0.4, 0.11]\n          - [residual, 12.9, 16.8, 14.2, 14.6, 2.0, 0.14]\n\n      - title: \"Table 6: G-Coefficient Stability Across Item Samples\"\n        columns: [Metric, Sample_0, Sample_7, Sample_99, Mean, CV]\n        rows:\n          - [\"G (binary, practical)\", 0.614, 0.498, 0.581, 0.564, 0.11]\n          - [\"G (binary, all random)\", 0.591, 0.472, 0.558, 0.540, 0.11]\n          - [\"Items for G≥0.80 (practical)\", 410, 586, 462, 486, 0.19]\n\n    figures_description:\n      - >-\n        Forest plot: 3个item样本的item_id点估计 + 95% bootstrap CI，\n        标注overall mean和CV。展示中等变异性——置信区间有交叉但非完全重叠。\n\n    analysis: >-\n      CV=0.13表明item_id主导性对item选择有中等敏感性，但方向一致——所有3个样本中item_id均为最大方差源。\n      论文需要：(a) 以区间而非单点报告item_id（\"55-65% across item resamples\"），\n      (b) 讨论sample_7的49.3%为何偏低（item难度分布更均匀），\n      (c) 将resampling CV纳入D-study推算的不确定性。\n      对headline claim的影响：不改变定性结论（item dominance成立），但定量精度降低。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-002: Multi-Benchmark Replication\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Multi-Benchmark Replication (GSM8K, ARC, HellaSwag)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    status: completed\n    description: >-\n      4 models × BF16/FP16 × 6 prompts × 6 seeds × 2 temperatures × 4 orderings × 200 items\n      on GSM8K, ARC-Challenge, HellaSwag。Gemma使用BF16/FP32替代BF16/FP16。\n      测试跨benchmark方差梯度。\n    expected_results:\n      total_records: 1382400\n      records_per_benchmark: 460800\n      conditions_per_model_per_benchmark: 576\n\n      # Per-benchmark single-model average (across 4 models)\n      benchmark_results:\n        MMLU:\n          accuracy_mean: 0.689\n          item_id_pct: 59.7\n          prompt_x_item_pct: 4.8\n          seed_x_item_pct: 4.6\n          temp_x_item_pct: 3.5\n          precision_x_item_pct: 5.0\n          residual_pct: 14.7\n          single_model_G: 0.598\n          cross_model_G: 0.152\n          model_x_item_pct: 16.4\n          infra_x_method_binary_pct: 0.08\n        HellaSwag:\n          accuracy_mean: 0.635\n          item_id_pct: 54.2\n          prompt_x_item_pct: 5.8\n          seed_x_item_pct: 4.1\n          temp_x_item_pct: 4.5\n          precision_x_item_pct: 3.8\n          residual_pct: 17.2\n          single_model_G: 0.548\n          cross_model_G: 0.186\n          model_x_item_pct: 13.8\n          infra_x_method_binary_pct: 0.15\n        ARC_Challenge:\n          accuracy_mean: 0.553\n          item_id_pct: 41.8\n          prompt_x_item_pct: 10.5\n          seed_x_item_pct: 5.2\n          temp_x_item_pct: 5.8\n          precision_x_item_pct: 4.2\n          residual_pct: 21.5\n          single_model_G: 0.421\n          cross_model_G: 0.108\n          model_x_item_pct: 19.5\n          infra_x_method_binary_pct: 0.42\n        GSM8K:\n          accuracy_mean: 0.443\n          item_id_pct: 43.5\n          prompt_x_item_pct: 8.9\n          seed_x_item_pct: 5.5\n          temp_x_item_pct: 7.2\n          precision_x_item_pct: 3.6\n          residual_pct: 22.8\n          single_model_G: 0.438\n          cross_model_G: 0.125\n          model_x_item_pct: 18.1\n          infra_x_method_binary_pct: 0.65\n\n      # Gradient analysis\n      gradient:\n        item_id_order_observed: [MMLU, HellaSwag, GSM8K, ARC_Challenge]\n        item_id_order_expected: [MMLU, HellaSwag, ARC_Challenge, GSM8K]\n        anomalous_benchmark: ARC_Challenge\n        anomaly_direction: \"ARC item_id异常偏低（41.8% vs 预期>GSM8K的43.5%）\"\n        item_id_spread_pp: 17.9\n        gradient_rank_correlation: 0.80\n\n      # Separability across benchmarks (binary)\n      separability_binary:\n        MMLU: 0.08\n        HellaSwag: 0.15\n        ARC_Challenge: 0.42\n        GSM8K: 0.65\n\n    result_rationale: >-\n      跨benchmark梯度反映了不同任务类型的item难度变异结构差异。\n      MMLU（知识检索）item_id最高（59.7%）：因为factual knowledge items的难度\n      在条件变化下高度稳定——一个化学知识要么知道要么不知道，prompt措辞影响有限。\n      HellaSwag（常识NLI）item_id次高（54.2%）：commonsense completion的难度相对稳定，\n      但prompt format对NLI-style items有一定影响。\n      GSM8K（数学推理）item_id=43.5%：chain-of-thought推理引入更多随机性——\n      同一道数学题在不同temperature/prompt下可能走不同推理路径，\n      增加了temperature×item和prompt×item的方差份额。\n      ARC-Challenge（科学推理）item_id异常偏低（41.8%）：这是anomaly。\n      原因可能是ARC的科学题目对prompt措辞特别敏感（prompt×item=10.5%，远高于其他benchmark的4-6%），\n      因为scientific reasoning items的选项描述更复杂，措辞变化直接改变推理路径。\n      ARC的prompt sensitivity\"吸收\"了本应归属item_id的方差，导致item_id被压低。\n      分离性随task complexity增加而降低（MMLU=0.08% → GSM8K=0.65%），\n      但所有benchmark的binary infra×method交互均<1%，confirming separability在binary scoring下成立。\n\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 7: Cross-Benchmark Variance Decomposition (%, single-model average, binary correct)\"\n        columns: [Component, MMLU, HellaSwag, ARC, GSM8K]\n        rows:\n          - [item_id, 59.7, 54.2, 41.8, 43.5]\n          - [prompt_x_item, 4.8, 5.8, 10.5, 8.9]\n          - [seed_x_item, 4.6, 4.1, 5.2, 5.5]\n          - [temp_x_item, 3.5, 4.5, 5.8, 7.2]\n          - [precision_x_item, 5.0, 3.8, 4.2, 3.6]\n          - [ordering_x_item, 1.3, 2.2, 1.8, 1.2]\n          - [precision, 2.1, 1.8, 2.5, 1.5]\n          - [temperature, 1.7, 2.4, 2.7, 3.0]\n          - [other, 2.6, 3.8, 4.0, 4.0]\n          - [residual, 14.7, 17.2, 21.5, 22.8]\n\n      - title: \"Table 8: Cross-Benchmark Gradient Summary\"\n        columns: [Benchmark, TaskType, item_id_pct, single_G, cross_model_G, model_x_item_pct, separability_pct]\n        rows:\n          - [MMLU, knowledge, 59.7, 0.598, 0.152, 16.4, 0.08]\n          - [HellaSwag, commonsense, 54.2, 0.548, 0.186, 13.8, 0.15]\n          - [GSM8K, math_reasoning, 43.5, 0.438, 0.125, 18.1, 0.65]\n          - [\"ARC-Challenge*\", science_reasoning, 41.8, 0.421, 0.108, 19.5, 0.42]\n        note: \"* ARC-Challenge为anomalous benchmark：item_id低于GSM8K，打破expected gradient\"\n\n      - title: \"Table 9: Per-Benchmark D-Study — Items for G≥0.80 (single-model, practical)\"\n        columns: [Benchmark, items_G80_practical, items_G80_all_random, current_G_200items]\n        rows:\n          - [MMLU, 414, 510, 0.598]\n          - [HellaSwag, 488, 612, 0.548]\n          - [ARC-Challenge, 682, 845, 0.421]\n          - [GSM8K, 648, 798, 0.438]\n\n    figures_description:\n      - >-\n        Stacked bar chart: 4 benchmarks并排展示方差分解，item_id用深蓝色突出。\n        MMLU的深蓝色最高（59.7%），GSM8K和ARC最低（~42-44%），\n        prompt×item（橙色）在ARC中异常突出。标注anomaly注释。\n      - >-\n        Scatter plot: x轴=task complexity ordinal（knowledge→commonsense→science→math），\n        y轴=item_id%。标注expected monotonic gradient线和observed values。\n        ARC点明显偏离趋势线。\n\n    analysis: >-\n      梯度方向大致正确（知识任务item_id最高，推理任务最低），但ARC的异常打破了单调性。\n      对论文叙事的影响：不能使用\"systematic gradient\"或\"monotonic decrease\"——\n      改为\"suggestive evidence of benchmark-conditional variance structure\"，\n      并专门讨论ARC异常的原因（prompt sensitivity absorbing item variance）。\n      积极方面：跨benchmark的separability一致低于1%（binary），confirming Claim 2的核心结论。\n      D-study预算因benchmark而异（414-682 items for G≥0.80），证明universal budget不可行——\n      这本身是一个有价值的finding。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-003: Multi-Hardware G-Study (INCOMPLETE)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Multi-Hardware G-Study\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    status: incomplete\n    description: >-\n      第二块GPU未到位（Manager审批延迟 + 云GPU成本超预算）。\n      仅有westd-32570 (RTX PRO 6000) 上的precision变异数据，\n      与exp-001完全冗余——无法计算hardware × methodology交互。\n    expected_results:\n      completion_pct: 0\n      usable_data_beyond_exp001: none\n      hardware_types_available: 1\n      hardware_x_methodology_computable: false\n      precision_x_methodology_from_exp001: available\n      planned_records: 1382400\n      actual_records: 0\n\n    result_rationale: >-\n      exp-003的核心价值是hardware crossing——测试不同GPU架构对方差结构的影响。\n      无第二种GPU，所有数据均来自同一RTX PRO 6000，precision变异已由exp-001完整覆盖。\n      不存在\"部分完成\"——hardware facet要么有crossing，要么没有。\n      没有crossing意味着infrastructure facet在论文中只能被定义为\"numerical precision on single hardware\"，\n      hardware × methodology交互完全缺失。\n      这是median scenario的最大单一gap——直接影响Claim 2的scope和可信度。\n      Reviewer极可能质疑：\"如果只测了一种GPU上的precision变化，你的separability结论能推广到什么范围？\"\n\n    tables: []\n\n    figures_description: []\n\n    analysis: >-\n      exp-003缺失迫使Claim 2重新定义。原measures：\"infrastructure × methodology separability\"\n      变为\"numerical precision × methodology separability on a single GPU architecture (RTX PRO 6000)\"。\n      论文需要：(a) 将hardware crossing明确标注为future work，\n      (b) 引用Yuan et al. (2025)的multi-GPU结果作为间接支持，\n      (c) 在limitations中承认：\"我们的separability结论限于precision facet；\n      GPU架构差异可能引入额外的hardware × item交互，这需要后续研究验证。\"\n      对AAAI投稿的影响：Claim 2从\"confirmatory with novel infrastructure crossing\"\n      降级为\"confirmatory on a subset of infrastructure dimensions\"。\n      影响可控——separability本身就被定位为confirmatory finding而非primary novelty。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-004: Comprehensive Analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Comprehensive Analysis of Combined Data\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    status: completed\n    description: >-\n      整合exp-001/001b/002数据（exp-003缺失）的全面分析。\n      包含model-as-facet、bootstrap CIs、D-study、IRT对比等17个子分析。\n    expected_results:\n      data_sources: [exp-001, exp-001b, exp-002]\n      missing_data: exp-003\n\n      # (a) Model-as-facet (same as exp-001 cross-model results)\n      model_as_facet:\n        model_x_item_pct: 16.4\n        cross_model_G: 0.152\n\n      # (b) Bootstrap CIs (1000 resamples, MMLU 4-model)\n      bootstrap_CIs_95pct:\n        item_id: [36.8, 45.6]\n        model: [3.2, 10.4]\n        model_x_item: [11.2, 21.8]\n        precision: [0.6, 2.4]\n        prompt_x_item: [2.4, 5.2]\n        seed_x_item: [2.1, 4.9]\n        precision_x_item: [1.8, 4.6]\n        temp_x_item: [1.2, 3.6]\n        infra_x_method: [0.0, 0.4]\n        residual: [11.5, 17.9]\n\n      # (c) D-study with CIs\n      d_study_G80:\n        MMLU_practical: {point: 414, CI_95: [352, 498]}\n        MMLU_all_random: {point: 510, CI_95: [428, 618]}\n        HellaSwag_practical: {point: 488, CI_95: [405, 592]}\n        ARC_practical: {point: 682, CI_95: [558, 838]}\n        GSM8K_practical: {point: 648, CI_95: [532, 792]}\n\n      # (d) REML vs Henderson\n      reml_vs_henderson_max_diff_pct: 1.8\n\n      # (e) Logprob scoring\n      logprob_item_id_pct: 52.4\n      logprob_G: 0.528\n      logprob_note: \"item_id lower than binary (52.4% vs 59.7%) because logprob captures partial knowledge\"\n\n      # (h) IRT vs G-theory comparison\n      irt_vs_gtheory:\n        MMLU:\n          irt_items_recommended: 116\n          gtheory_items_G80_practical: 414\n          ratio: 3.6\n          gtheory_G_at_116_items: 0.489\n          gap_attribution:\n            prompt_x_item_pct: 4.8\n            seed_x_item_pct: 4.6\n            ordering_x_item_pct: 1.3\n            residual_pct: 14.7\n        HellaSwag:\n          irt_items_recommended: 108\n          gtheory_items_G80_practical: 488\n          ratio: 4.5\n          gtheory_G_at_108_items: 0.442\n        ARC:\n          irt_items_recommended: 98\n          gtheory_items_G80_practical: 682\n          ratio: 7.0\n          gtheory_G_at_98_items: 0.352\n        GSM8K:\n          irt_items_recommended: 105\n          gtheory_items_G80_practical: 648\n          ratio: 6.2\n          gtheory_G_at_105_items: 0.372\n        mean_ratio: 4.1\n\n      # (i) Power analysis\n      power_analysis:\n        design_scale: \"5184 conditions × 200 items per benchmark\"\n        detectable_interaction_pct: 0.5\n        power_at_1pct_interaction: 0.99\n        power_at_0.3pct_interaction: 0.92\n\n      # (k) Fixed vs random sensitivity\n      fixed_vs_random:\n        temp_fixed_G_change: 0.032\n        ordering_fixed_G_change: 0.018\n        max_variance_shift_pct: 3.2\n        conclusion: \"robust (<5% threshold)\"\n\n      # (l) Binary data analysis\n      binary_data:\n        bernoulli_correlation_r: 0.38\n        bernoulli_p_value: \"<0.001\"\n        obs_over_bernoulli_ratio: 1.0008\n        null_sim_item_id_pct: 0.08\n        observed_item_id_pct: 59.7\n        inflation_factor: 746.3\n\n      # (m) Bootstrap vs jackknife\n      bootstrap_vs_jackknife:\n        CI_width_ratio_range: [0.94, 1.08]\n        mean_ratio: 1.01\n        conclusion: \"independence violation negligible\"\n\n      # (n) Design asymmetry sensitivity\n      design_asymmetry:\n        MMLU_3x3_item_id: 59.7\n        MMLU_2x2_matched_item_id: 58.9\n        max_component_change_pct: 2.1\n        conclusion: \"robust to design reduction\"\n\n      # (o) Full benchmark projection\n      full_benchmark:\n        MMLU_14K_items_G_practical: 0.942\n        MMLU_14K_items_G_all_random: 0.871\n\n      # (q) GPU cost analysis\n      gpu_cost:\n        cost_per_G80_MMLU_practical_usd: 12.5\n        cost_per_G80_ARC_practical_usd: 28.4\n        note: \"based on A100-80GB cloud pricing at $2.50/hr\"\n\n    result_rationale: >-\n      Bootstrap CIs揭示了4-model分析的核心不确定性：model×item的CI为[11.2, 21.8]，\n      宽度10.6pp，这是因为只有4个models作为model facet的levels，degrees of freedom极低。\n      这意味着model×item的真实值可能低至11.2%（接近\"non-dominant\"）或高至21.8%（接近\"dominant\"）。\n      CI的宽度本身就是一个finding——它说明4个models不足以精确估计model×item。\n      IRT vs G-theory对比是最稳健的分析（不依赖model facet），MMLU上的3.6×差距\n      直接归因于prompt×item(4.8%), seed×item(4.6%), ordering×item(1.3%)和residual(14.7%)——\n      这些维度是IRT完全忽略的。跨benchmark的ratio从3.6×（MMLU）增加到7.0×（ARC），\n      因为reasoning tasks的prompt/seed sensitivity更高，使G-theory和IRT的gap进一步扩大。\n      Fixed vs random sensitivity分析确认facet分类对方差分解影响<5%，\n      这是对MD2审稿问题的直接回答。\n      Bernoulli correlation r=0.38意味着item_id中约14%的变异（r²=0.14）可归因于Bernoulli p(1-p)——\n      这是non-trivial但不dominant的mechanical link，大部分item方差反映了真实的item difficulty异质性。\n\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 10: Bootstrap 95% CIs for MMLU 4-Model Variance Components (%)\"\n        columns: [Component, Point_Est, CI_Low, CI_High, CI_Width]\n        rows:\n          - [item_id, 41.2, 36.8, 45.6, 8.8]\n          - [model, 6.8, 3.2, 10.4, 7.2]\n          - [model_x_item, 16.4, 11.2, 21.8, 10.6]\n          - [precision, 1.5, 0.6, 2.4, 1.8]\n          - [prompt_x_item, 3.8, 2.4, 5.2, 2.8]\n          - [seed_x_item, 3.5, 2.1, 4.9, 2.8]\n          - [precision_x_item, 3.2, 1.8, 4.6, 2.8]\n          - [temp_x_item, 2.4, 1.2, 3.6, 2.4]\n          - [infra_x_method, 0.08, 0.0, 0.4, 0.4]\n          - [residual, 14.7, 11.5, 17.9, 6.4]\n\n      - title: \"Table 11: IRT vs G-theory Item Requirements for G≥0.80\"\n        columns: [Benchmark, IRT_items, Gtheory_items_practical, Ratio, Gtheory_G_at_IRT_items]\n        rows:\n          - [MMLU, 116, 414, \"3.6×\", 0.489]\n          - [HellaSwag, 108, 488, \"4.5×\", 0.442]\n          - [GSM8K, 105, 648, \"6.2×\", 0.372]\n          - [ARC-Challenge, 98, 682, \"7.0×\", 0.352]\n          - [Mean, 107, 558, \"4.1×(MMLU/Hella), 5.3×(all)\"]\n\n      - title: \"Table 12: Methodological Defense Summary\"\n        columns: [Defense, Analysis, Result, Conclusion]\n        rows:\n          - [MD1, \"Bernoulli correlation\", \"r=0.38, r²=0.14\", \"partial mechanical link, not dominant\"]\n          - [MD2, \"Fixed vs random\", \"max shift 3.2%\", \"robust (<5%)\"]\n          - [MD5, \"Full MMLU projection\", \"14K items → G=0.942\", \"subsampling is the cost, not MMLU flaw\"]\n          - [MD6, \"Bootstrap vs jackknife\", \"ratio 0.94-1.08\", \"independence violation negligible\"]\n          - [MD8, \"3×3 vs 2×2 matched\", \"max change 2.1%\", \"robust to design reduction\"]\n          - [MD9, \"Logprob scoring\", \"item_id=52.4%, G=0.528\", \"consistent direction, lower magnitude\"]\n\n      - title: \"Table 13: D-Study Budget — Items × Prompts × Seeds for Target G (MMLU, practical)\"\n        columns: [Target_G, Items, Prompts, Seeds, Total_Conditions]\n        rows:\n          - [0.80, 414, 1, 1, 414]\n          - [0.80, 280, 2, 2, 1120]\n          - [0.90, 685, 1, 1, 685]\n          - [0.90, 420, 2, 3, 2520]\n          - [0.95, 1050, 1, 1, 1050]\n          - [0.95, 610, 3, 3, 5490]\n\n    figures_description:\n      - >-\n        Figure 3: D-study projection curves — G vs item count for MMLU。\n        两条曲线：practical（precision+temp fixed）和all-random。\n        标注G=0.80 threshold和IRT推荐的116 items处的G值（0.489）。\n        标注差距区域（116→414 items）并label为\"cost of multi-facet reliability\"。\n      - >-\n        Figure 4: IRT vs G-theory bar chart — 4 benchmarks并排，\n        每个benchmark两个bar（IRT items vs G-theory items），ratio标注在bar上方。\n        高亮MMLU的3.6×到ARC的7.0×渐变，说明gap因benchmark而异。\n      - >-\n        Figure 5: Bootstrap CI forest plot — 所有方差组件的点估计 + 95% CI，\n        model×item的CI跨越\"substantial\"和\"moderate\"区域。\n\n    analysis: >-\n      exp-004是论文的analytical backbone。最关键的三个outputs：\n      (1) IRT vs G-theory的4.1×差距成为论文最强claim——不受model数量限制，\n      统计power充足，跨benchmark一致（3.6-7.0×），且有清晰的causal attribution\n      （prompt/seed/ordering维度IRT完全忽略）。建议提升为Contribution 1。\n      (2) Bootstrap CIs量化了model×item估计的不确定性——CI width 10.6pp\n      意味着论文不能声称\"precisely 16.4%\"，需使用\"approximately 12-22%\"。\n      (3) D-study预算表是toolkit的核心deliverable——直接给出benchmark-specific的\n      items × prompts × seeds组合和对应的expected G，填补了practical guidance的空白。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-005: 14B Model Extension (NOT COMPLETED)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"14B Model Extension\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    status: not_started\n    description: >-\n      未完成——需要第二种GPU（≥48GB VRAM）且依赖exp-003。\n      提供projected results用于论文Discussion中的future work section。\n    expected_results:\n      projected_if_completed:\n        models: [Qwen3-14B, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-14B]\n        item_id_range_pct: [52, 62]\n        model_x_item_change: \"potentially reduced by 2-4pp due to larger model capacity\"\n        scale_effect_hypothesis: >-\n          14B models may show lower model×item because larger capacity enables\n          more consistent item-level patterns across architectures.\n          Alternatively, specialized training (DeepSeek R1 distillation) could\n          increase model×item by creating architecture-specific item shortcuts.\n\n    result_rationale: >-\n      未执行因hardware constraint和dependency chain（exp-003→exp-005）。\n      即使有GPU，14B模型的推理时间约为8B的2-3×，120 GPU hours可能不够覆盖full design。\n      Projected results基于scale-accuracy关系的文献推断：\n      larger models通常在更多items上达到高准确率，这可能降低item-level variance\n      （更多items接近p=1.0，Bernoulli variance减少）。\n      但DeepSeek-R1-Distill的reasoning-specific训练可能创造独特的item difficulty profile，\n      增加model×item interaction。两种效应可能部分抵消。\n\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >-\n      exp-005缺失意味着scale-dependent结论无法做出。\n      论文需在limitations中声明：\"our findings are limited to 7-9B parameter models;\n      whether model×item interaction scales with model size is an open question.\"\n      这是可接受的scope limitation——大多数evaluation methodology papers不做scale analysis。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-006: Fine-Tuning G-Study (PARTIAL)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Fine-Tuning G-Study (RoBERTa, Partial)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    status: partial\n    description: >-\n      完成2/4 tasks（SST-2, MNLI）。仅1 GPU（非计划的3 GPU）。\n      6 seeds × 3 LRs × 4 data shuffles × 1 GPU × 2 precisions = 144 runs/task。\n      288 total runs（计划1728的16.7%）。\n    expected_results:\n      tasks_completed: [SST-2, MNLI]\n      tasks_missing: [RTE, COPA]\n      total_runs: 288\n      completion_pct: 16.7\n      gpu_facet_missing: true\n\n      SST2_variance_decomposition:\n        seed_pct: 31.5\n        learning_rate_pct: 22.3\n        data_shuffle_pct: 8.7\n        precision_pct: 2.4\n        seed_x_lr_pct: 6.2\n        seed_x_shuffle_pct: 3.8\n        lr_x_shuffle_pct: 4.1\n        precision_x_seed_pct: 1.5\n        other_pct: 2.8\n        residual_pct: 16.7\n      SST2_G_coefficient: 0.42\n      SST2_accuracy_mean: 0.938\n      SST2_accuracy_std: 0.008\n\n      MNLI_variance_decomposition:\n        seed_pct: 28.9\n        learning_rate_pct: 25.1\n        data_shuffle_pct: 11.2\n        precision_pct: 1.8\n        seed_x_lr_pct: 7.4\n        seed_x_shuffle_pct: 4.2\n        lr_x_shuffle_pct: 3.5\n        precision_x_seed_pct: 1.2\n        other_pct: 2.9\n        residual_pct: 13.8\n      MNLI_G_coefficient: 0.38\n      MNLI_accuracy_mean: 0.871\n      MNLI_accuracy_std: 0.012\n\n      inference_vs_finetuning_comparison:\n        dominant_source_inference: \"item_id (55-65%)\"\n        dominant_source_finetuning: \"seed (29-32%)\"\n        second_source_inference: \"model×item (12-20%) or residual\"\n        second_source_finetuning: \"learning_rate (22-25%)\"\n        qualitative_shift: \"fundamentally different variance hierarchies\"\n\n    result_rationale: >-\n      Fine-tuning与inference的方差结构质变源于根本机制差异。\n      Inference中item是唯一变化的measurement occasion——模型参数固定，\n      所以item difficulty heterogeneity主导方差。\n      Fine-tuning中模型参数本身在每次run中不同（seed决定initialization和optimizer trajectory），\n      使seed成为dominant source。Learning rate控制optimization aggressiveness——\n      高LR可能跳过细粒度pattern，低LR可能陷入不同local minima，\n      两者都导致最终模型在item level上的behavior差异。\n      Data shuffle影响training order exposure，MNLI（多分类，131K训练样本）比SST-2\n      （二分类，67K样本）更敏感于data ordering（11.2% vs 8.7%），\n      因为更大更复杂的训练集使得不同shuffle暴露不同的data pattern。\n      Precision在fine-tuning中影响小（1.8-2.4%）因为gradient accumulation平滑了numerical差异。\n      G=0.38-0.42意味着fine-tuning的reproducibility比inference更差——\n      即使固定learning rate和data，6个seeds产生的模型不够reliable。\n\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 14: Inference vs Fine-Tuning Variance Hierarchy Comparison (%)\"\n        columns: [Rank, Inference_Source, Inference_Pct, Finetuning_Source, Finetuning_Pct]\n        rows:\n          - [1, item_id, \"55-65\", seed, \"29-32\"]\n          - [2, \"residual\", \"13-23\", learning_rate, \"22-25\"]\n          - [3, \"precision×item\", \"3-6\", data_shuffle, \"9-11\"]\n          - [4, \"prompt×item\", \"4-6\", \"seed×lr\", \"6-7\"]\n          - [5, \"seed×item\", \"4-5\", \"lr×shuffle\", \"4-5\"]\n        note: \"Inference values averaged across 4 models on MMLU; fine-tuning averaged across SST-2/MNLI\"\n\n    figures_description:\n      - >-\n        Paired stacked bar: inference（左）vs fine-tuning（右）方差分解，\n        用颜色映射展示方差hierarchy的质变——inference中item_id的深蓝色主导，\n        fine-tuning中seed的红色主导。直观展示\"不同evaluation阶段的reproducibility瓶颈不同\"。\n\n    analysis: >-\n      部分fine-tuning结果的最大价值是展示\"方差hierarchy的阶段依赖性\"——\n      inference和fine-tuning面对完全不同的reproducibility瓶颈。\n      这为Contribution 4（toolkit）增加了新维度：practitioner需要不同的reproducibility budget\n      取决于他们是在evaluating还是training。\n      Caveats: (a) 仅RoBERTa（encoder-only），decoder fine-tuning可能完全不同；\n      (b) 仅1 GPU，GPU × seed交互未测试；(c) 2/4 tasks不够做task gradient analysis。\n      论文中应作为Discussion section的\"complementary evidence\"呈现，不作为独立claim。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-007: LayerCast (NOT COMPLETED)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"LayerCast Precision Mitigation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    status: not_started\n    description: >-\n      未完成——P2优先级，依赖exp-001。compute budget优先分配给P0/P1实验。\n    expected_results:\n      projected_if_completed:\n        layercast_precision_x_item_reduction: \"estimated 40-60% reduction vs pure fp16\"\n        layercast_G_improvement: \"estimated +0.02-0.05 over fp16 baseline\"\n        layercast_latency_overhead: \"~15-25% slower than pure fp16\"\n        note: \"projections based on LayerCast design (fp16 storage + fp32 compute)\"\n\n    result_rationale: >-\n      LayerCast通过在存储层使用fp16但计算层使用fp32来减少precision artifacts。\n      预计能减少precision×item交互40-60%，因为most numerical errors发生在compute layer\n      （矩阵乘法的cumulative rounding），而LayerCast在此处使用fp32。\n      但不能完全消除precision效应因为fp16 storage仍有representation precision loss。\n      作为mitigation strategy的价值在于提供\"actionable recommendation\"——\n      但缺失实验意味着这个recommendation只能作为speculation出现在Discussion中。\n\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >-\n      exp-007缺失对论文影响小——LayerCast是P2优先级的mitigation validation，\n      不影响核心claims。可在Future Work中提到：\"LayerCast and mixed-precision\n      strategies may reduce precision×item interaction; validation is ongoing.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-008: MATH Benchmark (NOT COMPLETED)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"MATH Benchmark Extension\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    status: not_started\n    description: >-\n      未完成——P2优先级，依赖exp-002。compute budget不足。\n    expected_results:\n      projected_if_completed:\n        item_id_pct: [35, 42]\n        prompt_x_item_pct: [10, 15]\n        temp_x_item_pct: [8, 14]\n        residual_pct: [22, 30]\n        single_model_G: [0.35, 0.42]\n        reasoning_variance_note: >-\n          MATH items involve multi-step proofs where chain-of-thought introduces\n          substantially more stochastic variance than GSM8K. Expected lowest\n          item_id of all benchmarks and highest temperature sensitivity.\n\n    result_rationale: >-\n      MATH是最强的reasoning benchmark——problems需要multi-step proof而非single-step arithmetic。\n      Chain-of-thought在每步引入branching possibilities，使得同一item在不同temperature/prompt下\n      走完全不同的reasoning path。这将temperature×item和prompt×item推到最高水平，\n      同时压低item_id。如果完成，MATH将是gradient的第5个点：\n      MMLU(60%) > HellaSwag(54%) > GSM8K(44%) > ARC(42%) > MATH(~38%)，\n      可能修复或加剧ARC anomaly。\n      缺失意味着gradient仅有4个benchmark，statistical power有限。\n\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >-\n      exp-008缺失使gradient分析限于4个benchmarks。如果MATH的item_id低于ARC（如projected），\n      ARC anomaly会更明显（ARC不在expected位置上），gradient叙事更难成立。\n      反之，如果MATH的item_id高于ARC，可能重新排列gradient使其更接近monotonic。\n      无论如何，4个benchmarks已足够支撑\"benchmark-conditional\"的结论——\n      不一定需要monotonic gradient，只需要证明variance structure因benchmark而异。\n```\n\n关键数值汇总对照：\n\n| 指标 | 本tier值 | 定义范围 |\n|---|---|---|\n| model×item (4-model) | 16.4% | [12, 20] |\n| cross-model G (4-model) | 0.152 | [0.10, 0.22] |\n| single-model item_id (mean) | 59.7% | [55, 65] |\n| benchmark item_id spread | 17.9pp | [10, 25] |\n| gradient rank corr | 0.80 | [0.4, 0.8] |\n| infra×method binary | 0.08% | [0.0, 1.0] |\n| IRT/G-theory ratio | 4.1× | [3.0, 4.5] |\n| resampling CV | 0.13 | [0.08, 0.18] |\n| P0 completed | 4/5 | [3, 4] |","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"4d478d45-0448-4f7e-a1b8-7636fa790f53","total_cost_usd":1.145129,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14970,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":41424,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14970,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":41424,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14970,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14970},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":9941,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.010036,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":41424,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":14970,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.1350930000000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"680990b3-a90e-47f2-9f65-d540eb7fb28e"}
